{"id":99760863507904,"type":"album","name":"Room on Fire","artist":"The Strokes","year":2003,"weight":25,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/room-on-fire-1.jpg","aoty":86,"aoty_user":84,"yt":"kaYk6pQd-Fk","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-strokes/room-on-fire","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/586-the-strokes-room-on-fire.php"},"desc":"Room on Fire is the second studio album by American indie rock band The Strokes. Released in October 2003, it follows 2001's Is This It and includes three singles: \"12:51\", \"Reptilia\", and \"The End Has No End.\" Grammy-winning producer Nigel Godrich was initially in charge of production, but The Strokes felt he made the songs seem \"soulless\". The band went back to work with Is This It producer Gordon Raphael. The album features a slightly smoother sound than its predecessor. The bass guitar is less present except for several moments when it becomes the focal point of the song. The ."},"artist_ref":{"id":157754209391560,"name":"The Strokes","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/TheStrokes.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":226054802434556,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":755,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":207419651019004,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":556,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":40264566616896,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Punk Revival","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":230,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":111142737429957,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Rock Revival","artist":null,"year":null,"weigh